<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belgian Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a>–<a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belgian Revolution was the uprising of 1830–1831 in which the southern provinces of the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a> broke away from King William I. It began with riots in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> after a performance of the opera La muette de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portici">Portici</a> in August 1830, and a provisional government declared independence in October. The great powers recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> in 1831 under King Leopold I, and the Netherlands accepted it in 1839.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belgian-revolution.jpg" alt="Belgian Revolution" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustaaf Wappers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustave_Wappers_-_%C3%89pisode_des_Journ%C3%A9es_de_septembre_1830_sur_la_place_de_l%27H%C3%B4tel_de_Ville_de_Bruxelles.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
